        "abstract": "In this article, we theoretically simulated a silicon core-based fiber Bragg grating and applied for temperature and environmental refractive index sensing simultaneously. The sensitivities of the temperature and refractive index were 79.25 <tex xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">$\\text{pm}/^{\\mathrm{o}}\\mathrm{C}$</tex> and -91.24 <tex xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">$\\text{dB}/\\text{RIU}$</tex>, respectively, within a range of the temperature in 0 to 45 <tex xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">${^\\circ C}$</tex> and the refractive index in 1.0 to 1.4. The proposed fiber sensor head can provide a method with simple and high sensitivity for various sensing target.",
